TITLE:: SequencerDocument
SUMMARY:: Encapsulates reading and writing sequencer source in a Document.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Document, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/WriteCommand, Classes/PatternText

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: composes a LINK::Classes/Document:: and is the place that knows how sequencer source is laid out: how to find MIDI parts, where to write new pattern text, and where to write the arranger's CODE::Seq().arrange:: call.

LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::, LINK::Classes/SequencerGui::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand:: talk to this class rather than to LINK::Classes/Document:: directly. Callers of LINK::#-insertPattern:: do not choose the insertion point; TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: owns that policy.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: wrapping the given LINK::Classes/Document::.

ARGUMENT:: document
The LINK::Classes/Document:: that holds sequencer source. LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: passes the LINK::Classes/Sequencer::'s document.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: insertPattern
Inserts pattern source into the composed LINK::Classes/Document::. The insertion location is chosen by TELETYPE::SequencerDocument::; callers do not specify it.

ARGUMENT:: string
The pattern source text to insert.

RETURNS::
This instance.

METHOD:: writeChipOrigins
Replaces the last CODE::Seq().arrange:: call in the document with one built from CODE::origins::. When there is no such call, appends a trailer. The rest of the file is left as it is. Keys are sorted by CODE::asString::. An id whose string contains a space is written in single quotes. The text is not evaluated.

ARGUMENT:: origins
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: of LINK::Classes/Symbol:: to LINK::Classes/Point::.

RETURNS::
This instance.

PRIVATE:: init, prIndexForInsert, prArrangeCall, prArrangeCallRange, prArrangeTrailer, prEndOfCall, prIsWhitespace, prReplaceRange, prSymbolText, prTextWithChipOrigins
